+Title: Avis Budget Group — Aegis AI platform Pilot: Provenance & Enforcement (8 weeks)
+Sponsor: Avis Product / ML / Security
+Duration: 8 weeks
+Objective:
+- Demonstrate end-to-end model provenance and enforced deployment controls for a revenue or safety-impacting model (example: dynamic pricing or predictive maintenance).
+- Produce audit-ready evidence (attestations + evidence bundles), enforce pre-load checks, and run Gatekeeper dry-run → enforcement flip.
+
+Scope & Deliverables
+- CI templates (OIDC -> Vault), GitHub Actions workflow that builds, signs (Vault Transit), publishes Rekor entry, and generates evidence bundle attached to MLflow.
+- Receipt_signer setup (configured to use Vault Transit) and Rekor instance (TLS + Postgres).
+- Evidence-bundle generator integrated with MLflow.
+- Pre-load attestation webhook deployed and integrated with the Avis serving fleet (cloud + edge pattern).
+- Gatekeeper constraint template for Avis namespaces; 72h dry-run and remediation automation.
+- Pilot runbook, acceptance tests and compliance packet for Avis auditors.
+
+Timeline & Milestones
+- Week 0: Kickoff, define pilot model and dataset, map owners and infra.
+- Week 1: Provision Avis pilot namespace (avis-aegis), deploy Rekor (TLS + Postgres) and Vault (BYOK option), configure CI OIDC role.
+- Week 2: Receipt_signer deployed + sample sign tests; evidence bundle pipeline added to CI.
+- Week 3: Pre-load webhook deployed and integrated with serving; MLflow evidence attachments validated.
+- Week 4: Gatekeeper policies applied in dry-run; collect violations & remediate.
+- Week 5: End-to-end test: commit -> CI sign -> Rekor entry -> deploy -> pre-load passes.
+- Week 6: Edge device test (offline fetchtoken + verification) on representative agent(s).
+- Week 7: Compliance packet assembled (evidence mapping to GDPR/SOC2), runbook finalization, pentest scheduling.
+- Week 8: Pilot wrap, metrics report, next steps (scale vs dedicated tenancy).
+
+Success criteria (acceptance)
+- Attestation coverage: >= 95% of promoted pilot models have valid attestation & evidence bundle in staging.
+- Signer latency: signer P95 < 5s (demo env target).
+- Enforcement: Gatekeeper dry-run completed 72h with remediation; enforcement flip tested in staging and can rollback within 15 minutes.
+- Edge validation: agent successfully verifies signed model and loads on-device; offline reconciliation tested.
+
+KPIs to report
+- Models promoted/day, commit → live median latency, attestation coverage %, signer latency P95, model_load_success_rate (cloud/edge), Gatekeeper violation count.
+
+Risks & mitigations
+- Key custody concern — offer BYOK (customer KMS) and dedicated Vault instance.
+- Gatekeeper false positives — dry-run + remediation automation + temporary bypass annotation.
+- Edge connectivity — offline fetchtoken flow + TTL + reconciliation.
+
+Staffing & Roles
+- Platform/SRE (owner): infra/deployment and monitoring
+- Security: Vault/keys policy + pentest coordination
+- ML: model selection, MLflow runs, validation tests
+- Product: pilot acceptance, business KPIs
+- Legal/Compliance: acceptance of evidence formats
+
+Next steps to start
+1. Confirm pilot model & dataset (pricing OR maintenance).  
+2. Approve resource budget and tenant type (managed vs dedicated).  
+3. Assign owners and schedule Week 0 kickoff.
+
