+# Runbook: Deploying Avis Pilot (Aegis AI platform)
+
+Prereqs:
+- Kubernetes cluster(s) for cloud pilot + test edge devices
+- DNS entries for Rekor (rekor.avis.example.com) and Vault if accessible
+- Vault KMS key (customer BYOK option) or cloud KMS
+- GitHub Actions OIDC trust configured to Vault
+
+1) Create namespaces
+ - kubectl create ns avis-aegis
+ - kubectl create ns avis-edge
+
+2) Deploy Rekor (k8s/rekor/rekor-deployment-tls.yaml) and configure `rekor-db` secret.
+3) Deploy Vault per runbook_vault_production.md or use an approved customer Vault.
+4) Deploy receipt_signer configured to use `avis-aegis` transit key (update config.example).
+5) Deploy pre-load webhook (services/attestation/preload_webhook_avis.py) as a Deployment/Service in `avis-aegis`.
+6) Deploy Gatekeeper ConstraintTemplate & Constraint in dry-run mode (gatekeeper/avis-signed-models-constraint.yaml).
+7) Configure CI secrets (VAULT_ADDR, VAULT_OIDC_ROLE, REKOR_URL, MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI) and run .github/workflows/avis_ci_sign_publish.yml on a test repo.
+8) Validate: commit sample model to repo -> CI sign -> Rekor entry -> evidence bundle -> MLflow attachment -> attempt deployment to avis-aegis namespace (pre-load webhook authorizes).
+9) Run Gatekeeper dry-run collector and remediation: gatekeeper/dryrun/collect_violations.sh -> gatekeeper/dryrun/remediate_violations.py
+10) Edge test: deploy avis-edge-agent DaemonSet and run offline_fetchtoken.sh to simulate device fetch & verify.
+
+Acceptance tests:
+- Successful end-to-end signed model deployment in avis-aegis namespace.
+- Gatekeeper dry-run violations collected and remediated.
+- Edge device loads signed model and verifies Rekor proof.
+- Compliance packet artifacts exported.
